		'correct_option' => 'a',
		'explanation' => "A. Correct. These are the core initiation duties stated in 16 CCR 1815.5(c), in addition to other applicable informed-consent and privacy requirements.\n\nB. Incorrect. California requires the consent process and documentation, not a specific form title.\n\nC. Incorrect. The initiation duties apply when telehealth services are initiated.\n\nD. Incorrect. Platform security and emergency planning do not replace the listed BBS initiation duties.\n\nCTA Exam Strategy: Identify authority, consent/confidentiality/privilege, the exact requester or decision-maker, and the required sequence before disclosing or acting.",
	),
	array(
		'question_text' => 'During a counseling session, an APCC working under supervision develops reasonable suspicion that a child has been abused. The clinic director asks the APCC to wait until tomorrow\'s team meeting so the agency can decide whether to report. What should occur FIRST?',
		'option_a' => 'Wait for the director because supervisors control agency reporting decisions.',
		'option_b' => 'Investigate until the APCC can prove that abuse occurred.',
		'option_c' => 'Make the mandated report immediately or as soon as practicably possible and complete the written follow-up within the statutory period; internal procedures may not delay the individual duty.',
		'option_d' => 'Document the concern internally and allow the director to make the external report.',
		'correct_option' => 'c',
		'explanation' => "A. Incorrect. Supervisors may not impede an individual mandated reporter's duty.\n\nB. Incorrect. Reasonable suspicion, not proof, is the reporting threshold.\n\nC. Correct. Penal Code 11166 uses reasonable suspicion as the threshold, requires an initial report immediately or as soon as practicably possible and a written follow-up within 36 hours, and makes the reporting duty individual.\n\nD. Incorrect. Internal notice does not substitute for the mandated report.\n\nCTA Exam Strategy: Identify the legal threshold, who has the duty, the required timing or protective step, and the narrow scope of any disclosure.",
	),
	array(
		'question_text' => 'An LPCC in an outpatient community clinic reasonably suspects financial abuse of an older adult client. The suspected abuse did not occur in a long-term-care facility, state mental hospital, or state developmental center. What is the BEST reporting sequence?',
		'option_a' => 'Notify the client\'s family and let them decide whether to contact authorities.',
		'option_b' => 'Report immediately or as soon as practicably possible to adult protective services or local law enforcement and, if the initial report is by telephone, send the required written report or confidential internet report within two working days.',
