		'option_d' => 'Report only to the client\'s bank because the concern is financial.',
		'correct_option' => 'b',
		'explanation' => "A. Incorrect. Family consultation does not replace the mandated reporter's statutory duty.\n\nB. Correct. WIC 15630 requires prompt reporting and specifies the agency and follow-up timing for abuse occurring outside the special facility categories.\n\nC. Incorrect. Mandated reporting does not require proof beyond the statutory reporting threshold.\n\nD. Incorrect. The statutory reporting pathway is to APS or local law enforcement for this setting.\n\nCTA Exam Strategy: Identify the legal threshold, who has the duty, the required timing or protective step, and the narrow scope of any disclosure.",
	),
	array(
		'question_text' => 'An LPCC\'s client communicates a serious threat of physical violence against a specifically identified former supervisor and describes access to a weapon. What is the BEST response?',
		'option_a' => 'Warn only the client\'s family because they know the client best.',
		'option_b' => 'Assess immediacy and safety, take the protective actions required by California law, including reasonable efforts to communicate the threat to the identifiable victim and law enforcement when the statutory conditions are met, and document the response.',
