	array(
		'question_text' => 'An LPCC evaluates a client who appears unable to provide for basic personal safety because of a severe mental disorder. The LPCC is not personally designated by the county to initiate a 5150 detention. What should the LPCC do FIRST?',
		'option_a' => 'Tell the client to return later if basic-needs problems continue for 72 hours.',
		'option_b' => 'Complete a 5150 application solely because the LPCC holds a California license.',
		'option_c' => 'Assess and document the factual risk, determine whether emergency evaluation is indicated, and activate the appropriate authorized county or emergency pathway rather than assuming detention authority the LPCC does not have.',
		'option_d' => 'Avoid emergency consultation because involuntary care is outside counseling practice.',
		'correct_option' => 'c',
		'explanation' => "A. Incorrect. The decision depends on current risk and legal criteria, not an arbitrary waiting period.\n\nB. Incorrect. Licensure alone does not automatically confer county-designated detention authority.\n\nC. Correct. Crisis reasoning separates clinical assessment from legal authority. Section 5150 detention authority belongs to persons authorized by statute/county designation; the LPCC should protect the client while using the lawful pathway.\n\nD. Incorrect. An LPCC still has responsibility to assess risk and coordinate appropriate emergency care within role.\n\nCTA Exam Strategy: Identify the legal threshold, who has the duty, the required timing or protective step, and the narrow scope of any disclosure.",
	),
	array(
		'question_text' => 'Two mandated reporters jointly learn facts creating reasonable suspicion of child abuse and agree that one of them will make the report. What remains true for the other reporter?',
		'option_a' => 'If the designated reporter fails to make the report, the other mandated reporter who knows of the failure must make the report.',
		'option_b' => 'The other reporter must always make a duplicate report even after confirming the designated report was made.',
		'option_c' => 'Only the supervisor may decide whether a team report counts.',
		'option_d' => 'The other reporter has no further responsibility once the team agrees on a reporter.',
		'correct_option' => 'a',
		'explanation' => "A. Correct. Penal Code 11166 permits a jointly selected reporter in specified circumstances but preserves individual responsibility when a designated reporter fails.\n\nB. Incorrect. A single jointly selected report may satisfy the reporting method when the statutory conditions are met.\n\nC. Incorrect. The reporting rules are statutory and the duty is individual; supervisor permission is not the controlling factor.\n\nD. Incorrect. The statute preserves a duty to act if the designated reporter fails.\n\nCTA Exam Strategy: Identify the legal threshold, who has the duty, the required timing or protective step, and the narrow scope of any disclosure.",
	),
	array(
		'question_text' => 'An LPCC must make a legally authorized safety disclosure. Which principle BEST guides how much confidential information to disclose?',
		'option_a' => 'Disclose the information reasonably necessary for the lawful protective purpose and avoid unrelated treatment details.',
		'option_b' => 'Release the entire record whenever any confidentiality exception applies.',
