		'correct_option' => 'd',
		'explanation' => "A. Incorrect. Privilege and disclosure are governed by legal authority, not the therapist's preference between litigants.\n\nB. Incorrect. California Evidence Code includes specific exceptions.\n\nC. Incorrect. Filing litigation does not create a universal automatic waiver of every confidential communication.\n\nD. Correct. Psychotherapist-patient privilege is strong but subject to defined exceptions and waiver rules. The proper response is issue-specific legal analysis rather than an absolute rule.\n\nCTA Exam Strategy: Identify the legal threshold, who has the duty, the required timing or protective step, and the narrow scope of any disclosure.",
	),
	array(
		'question_text' => 'An APCC creates a professional directory profile that lists only "Jordan Lee, APCC" and a registration number. Which correction is BEST under the advertising rule operative April 1, 2026?',
		'option_a' => 'Remove all online advertising because APCCs may never advertise.',
		'option_b' => 'Keep the profile unchanged because a registration number alone proves supervised status.',
		'option_c' => 'Include the Board-filed first and last name, complete registration title when using APCC, registration number, employer or volunteer entity, and a statement that the APCC is supervised by a licensed person.',
