		'correct_option' => 'c',
		'explanation' => "A. Incorrect. Registrants may advertise when the applicable requirements are met.\n\nB. Incorrect. The regulation requires more than a number and does not allow supervised status to be inferred.\n\nC. Correct. 16 CCR 1811 requires identity, title, number, and additional employer/entity and supervised-status information for registrants; the APCC abbreviation has a complete-title condition.\n\nD. Incorrect. Those are not the minimum advertising elements required by the regulation.\n\nCTA Exam Strategy: Separate professional status, lawful setting/scope, representation, documentation, and conduct requirements; consent cannot expand legal authority.",
