		'explanation' => "A. Incorrect. Independent-contractor mental-health practice is prohibited for an APCC.\n\nB. Incorrect. Client disclosure does not legalize a prohibited employment/payment arrangement.\n\nC. Correct. BPC 4999.46.3 prohibits independent-contractor practice for an APCC, direct remuneration from clients, and specified proprietary/rental arrangements; consultation is not a substitute for required supervision.\n\nD. Incorrect. The restrictions apply to the performance of professional services, not only to hours claimed for licensure.\n\nCTA Exam Strategy: Separate professional status, lawful setting/scope, representation, documentation, and conduct requirements; consent cannot expand legal authority.",
